Approved R2-1 correction
An alarm is no longer retained when this invocation suppresses its terminal warning because of a hold or cannot write it to stdout.
Invocation-local EXIT cleanup removes only the alarm created by this invocation on an undelivered exit; cleanup is disarmed after successful warning output.
The existing alarm, prior notice, budget, epoch and wake-queue owners are retained; no new coordinating state or locks were added.
No R1-2 coordination design or implementation was attempted.

Reproduction and verification
The exact alarm-release reproduction failed before production changes: held terminal output was empty, alarm=yes, and all three released auto-arms suppressed actionable delivery while pending counts grew 1/2/3.
After the correction, the held turn remains silent with no consumed alarm, and all three released auto-arms return exit 2 with actionable output while queued events survive.
The warning-first sequence retries and consumes a successfully delivered warning once.
The actionable-first sequence delivers and drains the latest same-key signal using existing coalescing semantics, while the terminal warning remains available.
Closed stdout returns its write error, keeps the warning unconsumed, and a successful retry consumes it.

